---
title: Player, supervisor and operator control
---
flowchart TD
  accTitle: Player proposes and the service controls execution
  accDescr: The user directs the lead and can Pause the controller. The lead admits a bounded task. A dedicated player sub-agent reads retained visible evidence and proposes a plan. The service validates that plan against fresh evidence and budgets, then a skill proposes one action and the controller checks its lease. The real game returns evidence and the spectator shows verified progress or uncertainty. The player has no raw-input role; agent instructions do not create an operating-system sandbox.
  User[You: objective and boundaries] --> Lead[Lead: task admission and supervision]
  Lead --> Task[One bounded task]
  Task --> Service[Run service: validate plan<br/>Fresh evidence and original budgets]
  Evidence[Retained visible observations] --> Player[Dedicated player sub-agent<br/>Proposes the next leg]
  Player -->|Candidate data only| Service
  Service --> Skill[Skill: propose and verify one step]
  Skill --> Controller[Controller: exact lease<br/>Deadline and native authority]
  Controller --> Game[Real windowed CDDA]
  Game --> Evidence
  Evidence --> Service
  Service --> Viewer[Spectator: verified progress<br/>Next check and stop reason]
  User -->|Pause revokes new input| Controller
